# 2026-09-13 (gen514) — full live KB; development probes, never persisted training.
# The pieces found by triaging the 33 open questions of the r300 prose ladder.
# Sentences are from that ladder or describe mechanics; no world fact of the
# ladder is stored in the KB.

[test the bare verb of an object question reaches a curated inflected relation]
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset
!timeout 60
> A coral reef is an underwater ecosystem. Coral belongs to the class Anthozoa in the animal phylum Cnidaria, which includes sea anemones and jellyfish.
<~ includes sea anemones
# «include» is the stem of the curated `includes`, and it closes the phrase
# («the phylum cnidaria», not «phylum_cnidaria_include»).
> what does the phylum cnidaria include?
<~ sea anemones

[test a bare plural describes the specific entity]
!reset
!timeout 30
> Shallow coral reefs occupy less than 0.1% of the world's ocean area.
<~ Learned
> what do reefs occupy?
<~ ocean area

[test a spoken construction can swap the roles]
!reset
!timeout 30
> Coral reefs are under threat from excess nutrients.
<~ Learned
> what threatens coral reefs?
<~ excess nutrients

[test a percentage without its connector is not a computation]
!reset
!timeout 30
> Reefs have declined by 50% since 1950.
<! 975
> what is 15% of 80?
<~ 12

[test the perfect is not possession]
!reset
!timeout 30
> Reefs have declined.
<! Learned
> what have reefs declined by?
<! Reefs
> Zelnik has a handle.
<~ Learned
> does zelnik have a handle?
<~ Yes

[test a piece of a phrase is not the thing asked]
!reset
!timeout 30
# The live KB holds provides(ocean, water): the question is about ocean waters.
> what do those ocean waters provide?
<! dissolved oxygen
> what does the ocean provide?
<~ water
